      "remaining": "Connect the adopted reference contract through FGO Lab canonical IR, shared execution, outcomes and recovery; verify relevant production cells and parity.",
      "historicalObservationRequirement": "Published description supports clamp-only but no discriminating before/after measurement was recovered. Removal must also be observed.",
      "referenceContract": {
        "commit": "9fa75655c07ecd76168b1ccf5b8232e8d64664cf",
        "rules": [
          "Maximum HP is max(base HP + fixed buff sum + trunc(0.001 * (rate buff sum * base HP)), 1), using the reference buff-action aggregation.",
          "For a living recipient, adding a maxhp/baseHp increase also gains current HP; adding a decrease loses the corresponding current HP amount with nonlethal lower bound 1. Percent changes use base HP, with integer conversion at the reference expression.",
          "Removing ordinary maxhp modifiers preserves current HP subject to the recomputed maximum; removing positive baseHp modifiers separately subtracts their contribution before clamping. Keep maxhp and baseHp categories distinct.",
          "Adopt 5000/10000 -> 3000/8000 for a 2000 ordinary maximum-HP reduction; removing that reduction gives 3000/10000. This is reference behavior, not an in-game measurement."
        ],
