      "protocol": "Use current HP 1 with the recorded legal maximum for the NP continuous-ratio branch. Separately test the same buff grant before and after healing and threshold H-1/H/H+1; retain owner and read clock. Damage observations must control or enumerate random rolls, not infer a one-unit coefficient from one random damage roll.",
      "remaining": "Connect the adopted reference contract through FGO Lab canonical IR, shared execution, outcomes and recovery; verify relevant production cells and parity.",
      "historicalObservationRequirement": "The earlier 1/11000 probe is schematic. A master-derived 1/13028 input is now provided, but no observation distinguishing integer-permille and continuous-ratio readers was recovered.",
      "referenceContract": {
        "commit": "9fa75655c07ecd76168b1ccf5b8232e8d64664cf",
        "rules": [
          "Buff HP conditions read the owner at use time: q = trunc((currentHP / maximumHP) * 1000), using double division/multiplication; HP_HIGHER and HP_LOWER compare q inclusively.",
          "HP-dependent buff values use that integer q, the declared min/max ratio range, clamping and truncation of the interpolated addition at BuffData.getValue. Keep the lower-bound contribution and upper-range behavior of the reference.",
          "HP-dependent NP coefficients use the current attacker HP / maximum HP ratio directly, without an intermediate integer permille: truncate((1-ratio)*Target) for low-HP and truncate(ratio*Target) for high-HP contributions.",
          "Display rounding, buff thresholds, NP coefficient rounding and HP0 reachability remain distinct. Do not import delegate HP overrides or let displayed 0% make a living actor dead."
        ],
